    "created_at": "2026-05-05T17:29:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-05T17:29:29Z",
    "body": "I think eventually `field-sizing` should have an `auto` value, which should be used by default for base appearance.\n\nSomething that should work like this maybe:\n- stretches the input to the full available inline size when display is block level (like a normal `<div>` element)\n- when display inline level, use the behavior of `field-sizing: content;` or `field-sizing: fixed` depending on the control (e.g. select could use `field-sizing: content`, but input could use `field-sizing: fixed` or something among those lines)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
